title: The Campaign
subtitle: Germany elects its first Reichstag on 6 June.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1920 and month = 5 and crisis = 0 and ending_id = 0
max-visits: 1
priority: 2

= The Campaign

The National Assembly has done its work, and the first Reichstag of the Republic will be elected on 6 June. [? if kapp_outcome = 3 : The workers' government hopes to win a majority of its own. The bourgeois parties campaign against "the dictatorship of Legien". ?][? if kapp_outcome != 2 and kapp_outcome != 3 : The coalition of the SPD, the Centre and the Democrats is tired and unloved. The nationalists campaign on the shame of Versailles, the Independents on the betrayal of the revolution. ?][? if kapp_outcome = 2 : The Republic that the Ruhr saved is holding its election under the shadow of the generals who nearly destroyed it. ?]

It is the first national election our party contests. We have few candidates anyone has heard of, little money and no daily paper in most of the Reich. [? if election_boycott = 1 : But the party has decided to boycott the vote. ?]

- @lessons: Campaign on the lessons of the Kapp days.
- @tribune: Campaign to use the Reichstag as a tribune for the revolution.
- @bloc: Call for a bloc of the workers' parties against the bourgeoisie.
- @boycott: Boycott the election.

@lessons
subtitle: The Spartacist campaign. Who saved the Republic, and who nearly lost it.
choose-if: lock_elections < 2 and election_boycott = 0
unavailable-subtitle: The party will not stand in this election.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e20_campaign = 1;
Q.election_bonus += 2;
Q.luxemburgist_satisfaction += 5;
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 2;
!}

Our posters show the Ehrhardt Brigade's helmets and the strikers who stopped them. Our speakers ask why the officers of March are still in their barracks.

@tribune
subtitle: The Left's campaign. The Reichstag is a stage, not a workplace.
choose-if: lock_elections < 2 and election_boycott = 0
unavailable-subtitle: The party will not stand in this election.
on-arrival: {!
Q.e20_campaign = 2;
Q.election_bonus += 1;
Q.militancy += 3;
Q.offensive_satisfaction += 6;
Q.lean_offensive += 2;
!}

We tell the voters plainly: our deputies will go to the Reichstag to denounce it, and to call the workers to the councils. Some workers like the honesty.

@bloc
subtitle: [? if lock_united_front = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] The Right's campaign. The USPD will like it; it may cost us votes to them.
choose-if: lock_elections < 2 and election_boycott = 0 and lock_united_front < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The party line does not allow it.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_united_front == 1) {
    Q.unity -= 10;
    Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10;
}
Q.e20_campaign = 3;
Q.election_bonus += 1;
Q.uspd_relation += 8;
Q.spd_relation += 3;
Q.uspd_score += 1;
Q.unionist_satisfaction += 6;
Q.lean_unionist += 2;
!}

Our speakers call for a workers' majority in the Reichstag, and for the SPD and USPD to break with the bourgeois parties for good. The USPD's speakers say kind things about us for the first time.

@boycott
subtitle: The Left Radical answer. No votes for parliament, not even our own.
view-if: ultraleft_gone = 0 or election_boycott = 1 or lock_elections = 2
on-arrival: {!
Q.e20_campaign = 4;
Q.election_boycott = 1;
Q.ultraleft_satisfaction += 10;
Q.luxemburgist_satisfaction -= 8;
Q.unionist_satisfaction -= 8;
Q.lean_ultraleft += 2;
!}

Our posters say: do not vote, organise in the factories. Most workers vote anyway, for the USPD.
